<div class="re-ai-editorial">
<section><h2>Connect Facebook leads to an AI-assisted response workflow</h2><p>When a prospect submits a Meta lead form, a CRM workflow can record the campaign and property interest, notify the assigned agent and send an appropriate acknowledgement where messaging consent allows. A clearly identified AI assistant can respond to basic questions about the promoted listing or the consultation process using approved information.</p><p>The automation should recognize the difference between a buyer inquiry, a homeowner asking about selling and someone requesting rental information. A single generic conversation is unlikely to be equally useful to all three.</p></section>
<section><h2>Use conversations to evaluate lead quality</h2><p>A low-cost lead form can produce many submissions without generating useful conversations. Review whether contacts recognize the offer, respond to follow-up and take meaningful next steps. AI call handling, missed-call recovery and agent notifications can support that process.</p><p>Housing advertising rules, fair housing obligations and appropriate messaging consent still apply. Automated conversations should not invent property availability, imply preferential treatment or count a booking request as a confirmed appointment.</p></section>
